    {
     "author": {
      "accountId": "6089a4f65432640068676436",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/8ce8452e767f2beb6aebffe0ef7cbc3e?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FGW-2.png",
       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/8ce8452e767f2beb6aebffe0ef7cbc3e?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FGW-2.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/8ce8452e767f2beb6aebffe0ef7cbc3e?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FGW-2.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/8ce8452e767f2beb6aebffe0ef7cbc3e?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FGW-2.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Graeme West",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=6089a4f65432640068676436",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>Hi there,<br/>\nI don't have a complete Fedora-Commons build environment set up quite yet, but I have implemented Steve's suggested changes against a checkout of the trunk.</p>\n\n<p>They work great. I tested with a 2.3GB file, and the hard limit is gone. An example log output is as follows:</p>\n\n<p>INFO 2010-05-25 15:38:31.162 <span class=\"error\">&#91;http-8080-1&#93;</span> (DefaultManagement) Completed getDatastream(pid: mydemo:1, datastreamID: bigmovie, asOfDateTime: null)<br/>\nINFO 2010-05-25 15:44:00.746 <span class=\"error\">&#91;http-8080-1&#93;</span> (DefaultDOManager) Committing modification of mydemo:1<br/>\nINFO 2010-05-25 15:44:00.748 <span class=\"error\">&#91;http-8080-1&#93;</span> (DefaultDOManager) Getting managed datastream from internal uploaded location: uploaded://1<br/>\nINFO 2010-05-25 15:45:28.965 <span class=\"error\">&#91;http-8080-1&#93;</span> (DefaultDOManager) Replaced managed datastream location with internal id: mydemo:1+bigmovie+bigmovie.0<br/>\nINFO 2010-05-25 15:45:28.989 <span class=\"error\">&#91;http-8080-1&#93;</span> (DefaultDOManager) Updating dissemination index<br/>\nINFO 2010-05-25 15:45:28.989 <span class=\"error\">&#91;http-8080-1&#93;</span> (DefaultDOManager) Updating FieldSearch index<br/>\nINFO 2010-05-25 15:45:28.994 <span class=\"error\">&#91;http-8080-1&#93;</span> (DefaultManagement) Completed addDatastream(pid: mydemo:1, dsID: bigmovie, altIDs: '', dsLabel: A large video file, versionable: true, MIMEType: video/mp4, formatURI: , dsLocation: uploaded://1, controlGroup: M, dsState: A, checksumType: Default, checksum: null, logMessage: null)</p>\n\n<p>Caveat:<br/>\nThe only niggle I can see is that the Flex interface does not give any visual feedback indicating that the file upload has completed - the little 'upload' window continues to display with an indefinite progress indicator, despite the addition of the datastream having already completed. However, testing indicates that this is the case regardless of the size of Managed Content datastream uploaded.</p>\n\n<p>I've attached a diff of the file /trunk/fcrepo-server/src/main/java/org/fcrepo/server/rest/RestUtil.java   which implements the change against version 8587 of the same file from the SVN.</p>\n\n<p>Hopefully this is of some help to those with commit privileges.</p>\n\n<p>Graeme</p>",
